{"id":"devlink-monitor.8","n":"devlink-monitor","s":"8","src":{"r":{"pkg":"iproute","ver":"6.11.0-1.el9","repo":"BaseOS","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/BaseOS/x86_64/os/Packages/i/iproute-6.11.0-1.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/devlink-monitor.8.gz","sha256":"c9775add91d65b00954e7714e1f3f184ea72f71332dac5e97f3e7050509ff4f8","date":"14 Mar 2016","origin":"iproute2"},"u":{"pkg":"iproute2","ver":"5.15.0-1ubuntu2.2","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/i/iproute2/iproute2_5.15.0-1ubuntu2.2_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/devlink-monitor.8.gz","sha256":"9e9d6354e9d32683e56191ef6638e37e73698daa9b7765e2563b38eff34b0890","date":"14 Mar 2016","origin":"iproute2"}},"nopt":{"r":0,"u":0},"desc":"state monitoring","same":true,"doc":[["NAME","<p>devlink-monitor - state monitoring</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<br> <p><b>devlink monitor</b> [ <b>all</b> | <i>OBJECT-LIST</i> ]</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>The <b>devlink</b> utility can monitor the state of devlink devices and ports continuously. This option has a slightly different format. Namely, the <b>monitor</b> command is the first in the command line and then the object list.</p> <p><i>OBJECT-LIST</i> is the list of object types that we want to monitor. It may contain <b>dev</b>, <b>port</b>, <b>health</b>, <b>trap</b>, <b>trap-group</b>, <b>trap-policer</b>.</p> <p><b>devlink</b> opens Devlink Netlink socket, listens on it and dumps state changes.</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>devlink</b>(8), <b>devlink-dev</b>(8), <b>devlink-sb</b>(8), <b>devlink-port</b>(8), <b>devlink-health</b>(8), <b>devlink-trap</b>(8),</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p>Jiri Pirko &lt;jiri@mellanox.com&gt;</p>"]]}